{"format":1,"key":"zone:hillsbrad","path":"/lore/zone/hillsbrad","name":"Hillsbrad Foothills","kind":"zone","label":"Zone","zone":{"key":"hillsbrad","name":"Hillsbrad Foothills","path":"/lore/zone/hillsbrad"},"levels":"Levels 20-30","description":"Hillsbrad Foothills is a green, fertile region that represents the last pastoral bastion of the fallen kingdom of Lordaeron. Despite having largely…","intro":[],"clips":[{"id":"zone:hillsbrad","part":"narration","anchor":"story","title":"The story","paras":["Hillsbrad Foothills is a green, fertile region that represents the last pastoral bastion of the fallen kingdom of Lordaeron. Despite having largely escaped the Scourge's plague, the land is torn apart by brutal open war between the humans of Southshore and the Forsaken entrenched at Tarren Mill. It serves as a violent crossroads where the armies of the Alliance and the Horde clash without mercy.","While northern Lordaeron rots under the blight of the Scourge, Hillsbrad remains strikingly green. Its rolling pastures, pine groves, and working farmsteads offer travelers a rare glimpse of what the kingdom looked like before the Third War. Yet that tranquil appearance is deceptive. The peaceful fields and rural roads are constantly swept by armed patrols, rogue mercenaries, and scavenger beasts. What should be Lordaeron's breadbasket has instead become its most contested borderland.","The political heart of Hillsbrad is defined by two entrenched strongholds. In the south along the coast lies Southshore, an Alliance haven populated by human refugees and soldiers fiercely loyal to the Alliance. To the north sits Tarren Mill, once a quiet human farming hamlet that was wiped out by the Scourge and later fortified as the Forsaken's southernmost garrison. The open ground between the two settlements is known throughout Azeroth as a relentless kill zone, where Alliance and Horde champions wage perpetual skirmishes for control of the region.","Hillsbrad's history of violence runs deep. During the Second War, its coast and hills witnessed the first massive clashes between the Grand Alliance and the Old Horde. Later, the fortress of Durnholde Keep served as the internment camp where Thrall was raised before leading the orcish rebellion. Today, Durnholde lies in ruins, seized by the Syndicate—displaced human nobles turned bandit cutthroats. Coastal murlocs, hostile gnolls, and the shadowed dead on Purgation Isle ensure that no corner of the hills is truly secure."],"hash":"3080e7","voices":{"male-narrator":{"sha":"1b7c6497c1","sec":114},"female-narrator":{"sha":"68203bfd44","sec":124}}}],"sources":[{"kind":"wiki","title":"Hillsbrad Foothills (Classic)","url":"https://warcraft.wiki.gg/wiki/Hillsbrad_Foothills_(Classic)"},{"kind":"wiki","title":"Hillsbrad Foothills","url":"https://warcraft.wiki.gg/wiki/Hillsbrad_Foothills"}],"related":[{"p":"/lore/subzone/southshore","n":"Southshore","k":"subzone"},{"p":"/lore/subzone/tarren-mill","n":"Tarren Mill","k":"subzone"},{"p":"/lore/subzone/durnholde-keep","n":"Durnholde Keep","k":"subzone"},{"p":"/lore/subzone/hillsbrad-fields","n":"Hillsbrad Fields","k":"subzone"},{"p":"/lore/subzone/dun-garok","n":"Dun Garok","k":"subzone"},{"p":"/lore/subzone/purgation-isle","n":"Purgation Isle","k":"subzone"},{"p":"/lore/zone/alterac","n":"Alterac Mountains","k":"zone"},{"p":"/lore/zone/arathi","n":"Arathi Highlands","k":"zone"},{"p":"/lore/npc/karos-razok","n":"Karos Razok","k":"npc"},{"p":"/lore/subzone/azurelode-mine","n":"Azurelode Mine","k":"subzone"},{"p":"/lore/subzone/chillwind-point","n":"Chillwind Point","k":"subzone"},{"p":"/lore/subzone/corrahn-s-dagger","n":"Corrahn's Dagger","k":"subzone"}],"children":[{"p":"/lore/subzone/azurelode-mine","n":"Azurelode Mine","k":"subzone"},{"p":"/lore/subzone/chillwind-point","n":"Chillwind Point","k":"subzone"},{"p":"/lore/subzone/corrahn-s-dagger","n":"Corrahn's Dagger","k":"subzone"},{"p":"/lore/subzone/darrow-hill","n":"Darrow Hill","k":"subzone"},{"p":"/lore/subzone